 "notes": "No deviation: one child, four batches, instrument checks passed (control success 0.542 over 2,048 cases, first batch 0.547; 30.9% eligible; untreated conversion 0.8%; between-slot eligibility agreement 0.894; 525 jointly eligible recapture pairs against a minimum of 300), 16,394 starts of an 18,000 ceiling. In-process diagnostic rollouts, not the fresh-process evaluator; authority only. RECAPTURE: +0.107 [+0.079, +0.134] paired sustained success among jointly eligible pairs (58 wins, 2 losses; batch-clustered [+0.052, +0.169]; Holm p < 0.001): the registered magnitude is supported. It FAILS the drop bound: paired drop difference +0.084, one-sided upper bound +0.104 against +0.05 (59 of 633 treated stuck episodes fall, median fall step 159, i.e. during the open-and-recatch), so it is not 'useful scripted authority' as registered. Post hoc, not registered: among the 574 treated episodes that are not dropped, 59% end with a mean final-second |axial rate| above 4 rad/s (median 5.6; 37% above 8; untreated 1.3%), but only 74 of 633 meet the strict sustained rule: the re-capture restarts rolling in most stuck episodes, and what is missing is retention during the manoeuvre and steadiness/centring afterwards. STROKE BOOST (1.5x for 60 steps): +0.019 [+0.007, +0.031], no drops, positive after Holm and across batches but below the registered magnitude: a small, safe lever. RESIDUAL x3 with a 0.30 cap: +0.006 [-0.003, +0.014]: tripling the learned residual does not release a stuck episode, so the 0.10 cap is not what binds. A null or a positive here bounds these three scripts at these settings (T0 = 120, 60 steps, one blend schedule), not every recovery action."
